BO_ 40 DRIVE_STATE_EXPERIMENTAL: 17 BMW_I3
 SG_ DRIVE_STATE_CYCLE_COMPAT : 0|2@1+ (1,0) [0|3] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ DRIVE_STATE_RAW : 8|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
  SG_ DRIVE_MODE_RAW : 24|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ DRIVE_STATE_GEAR_M3_COMPAT : 24|4@1+ (1,0) [0|15] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ DRIVE_STATE_P_LOCKED_M3_COMPAT : 49|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ DRIVE_STATE_KIND_BYTE_11 : 88|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ DRIVE_STATE_KIND_BYTE_14 : 112|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 CM_ BO_ 40 "Experimental drive-state frame. Cross-check against dynm BMW SP2018 FlexRay DBC shows this frame is the closest local match to their maybe_gear_switch frame, so helper signals for cycle_count, GEAR m3, and P_locked m3 are exposed here for analysis. Current i3 parked routes do not yet separate P/D/N/R robustly enough to use these helpers directly in CarState.";

BO_ 44 BRAKE_OR_REGEN_CANDIDATE_A: 17 BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_REGEN_STATE_A : 8|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_REGEN_STATE_B : 24|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 CM_ SG_ 44 BRAKE_REGEN_STATE_A "Experimental secondary longitudinal candidate. Across historical TJA routes 00000054/55 and modern ACC-only route 000000b3, this frame separates dynamic phases weakly but remains far less informative than 54 and 59 for manual pedal vs managed-following behavior.";

BO_ 54 BRAKE_BLEND_CANDIDATE_B: 17 BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_PHASE_BYTE_0 : 0|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_BLEND_STATE_A : 8|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_BLEND_STATE_B : 24|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_BLEND_STATE_C : 40|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_WORD_B : 24|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_WORD_C : 40|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_BLEND_BYTE_3 : 24|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_BLEND_BYTE_4 : 32|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_BLEND_BYTE_5 : 40|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ BRAKE_BLEND_BYTE_6 : 48|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_BYTE_4 : 32|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_BYTE_6 : 48|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
CM_ SG_ 54 BRAKE_BLEND_STATE_A "Primary brake-blend / regen-support candidate. Across 00000054, 00000055, modern ACC-only route 000000b3, and recent ACC-only route 00000147, this frame cleanly separates manual accelerator application, ACC armed/base, and managed/following phases. STATE_B and STATE_C rise strongly in managed-following and automatic decel windows. In 00000147, frame 54 becomes active in complementary subframes while 59 carries the powertrain-intent side, reinforcing that 54 is the best current stock longitudinal support frame for brake-blend / regen behavior rather than a standalone brake command.";
CM_ SG_ 54 LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_PHASE_BYTE_0 "Best current transport/phase byte for frame 54. Managed windows show a strong byte-level cycle with a counter-like low nibble, indicating housekeeping/phase structure rather than direct command magnitude.";
CM_ SG_ 54 LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_WORD_B "Best current negative-branch TX candidate. In managed ACC windows it is the dominant non-idle content when desired longitudinal behavior is decel / regen / brake-blend. Current conservative replay interpretation: use this family on the negative branch, primarily on odd/every-other managed subcycles, centered near 65025.";
CM_ SG_ 54 LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_WORD_C "Companion word to LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_WORD_B. Best current negative-branch TX candidate alongside frame 54 word B. Current conservative replay interpretation: use this family on the negative branch, primarily on odd/every-other managed subcycles, centered near 7.";
CM_ SG_ 54 LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_BYTE_4 "Low byte of the current best frame-54 negative-branch TX word. Useful for byte-local replay fitting and checksum/counter separation work.";
CM_ SG_ 54 LONG_TX_BRAKE_BLEND_BYTE_6 "Low byte of the current best frame-54 companion TX word. Useful for byte-local replay fitting and checksum/counter separation work.";

BO_ 59 PEDAL_OR_HOLD_STATE_CANDIDATE: 17 BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_PHASE_BYTE_0 : 0|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ PEDAL_HOLD_STATE_RAW : 16|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ PEDAL_HOLD_STATE_AUX : 32|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ PEDAL_HOLD_BYTE_2 : 16|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ PEDAL_HOLD_BYTE_3 : 24|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ PEDAL_HOLD_BYTE_4 : 32|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ PEDAL_HOLD_BYTE_5 : 40|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_WORD_B : 24|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_WORD_C : 40|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_BYTE_3 : 24|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_BYTE_5 : 40|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
CM_ SG_ 59 PEDAL_HOLD_STATE_RAW "Strongest stock longitudinal content candidate so far. Across 00000054, 00000055, 000000b3, and recent ACC-only route 00000147, RAW is high during clear manual accelerator application, lower in ACC armed/base, and lowest during managed/following windows. AUX also shifts strongly between manual and managed phases. In 00000147 managed ACC, 59 remains the dominant powertrain-intent family while 54 appears in complementary brake-blend subframes. This remains the best current candidate for stock pedal/hold/coast-state inference under ACC, not a closed accel command.";
CM_ SG_ 59 LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_PHASE_BYTE_0 "Best current transport/phase byte for frame 59. Managed windows show a strong byte-level cycle with a counter-like low nibble, indicating housekeeping/phase structure rather than direct command magnitude.";
CM_ SG_ 59 LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_WORD_B "Best current positive/coast TX candidate. In managed ACC windows it is the dominant non-idle content when desired longitudinal behavior is propulsion / hold / coast rather than brake-blend. Current conservative replay interpretation: use this family on the positive-or-coast branch, primarily on even/every-other managed subcycles, centered near 32777.";
CM_ SG_ 59 LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_WORD_C "Companion word to LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_WORD_B. Best current positive/coast TX candidate alongside frame 59 word B. Current conservative replay interpretation: use this family on the positive-or-coast branch, primarily on even/every-other managed subcycles, centered near 32767.";
CM_ SG_ 59 LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_BYTE_3 "Low byte of the current best frame-59 positive/coast TX word. Useful for byte-local replay fitting and checksum/counter separation work.";
CM_ SG_ 59 LONG_TX_POWERTRAIN_BYTE_5 "Low byte of the current best frame-59 companion TX word. Useful for byte-local replay fitting and checksum/counter separation work.";

BO_ 72 LAT_STOCK_TX_CANDIDATE: 17 BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_PHASE_BYTE_0 : 0|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_CNT_NIBBLE : 16|4@1+ (1,0) [0|15] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_CONST_F_NIBBLE : 20|4@1+ (1,0) [0|15] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_FLAG_BYTE_8 : 64|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
CM_ BO_ 72 "Primary lateral TX envelope candidate. Modern routes 000000e9, 000000ea, and managed-TJA route 00000176 strongly support src0/72 as the stock steering-control transmit family. Byte2 is not a steer command; it splits into a rolling low-nibble counter and a constant high nibble 0xF, while byte8 remains fixed at 0xE0. Historical dynm BMW SP2018 DBC also labels frame 72 as ACC steering control. Treat 72 as the outer TX phase/counter envelope; the actual steer content remains in frame 96.";
CM_ SG_ 72 LAT_STOCK_TX_PHASE_BYTE_0 "Primary outer phase/family byte for the stock lateral TX envelope. Use this for phase-local classification and parity/family splitting; do not treat it as direct steering magnitude.";
CM_ SG_ 72 LAT_STOCK_TX_CNT_NIBBLE "Rolling low-nibble counter observed inside the stock lateral TX envelope. Best current interpretation is a TX housekeeping counter, not steer magnitude.";
CM_ SG_ 72 LAT_STOCK_TX_CONST_F_NIBBLE "Constant high nibble 0xF in the lateral TX envelope byte pair. Treat as structural filler/format marker rather than command content.";
CM_ SG_ 72 LAT_STOCK_TX_FLAG_BYTE_8 "Structurally stable tail byte, usually 0xE0 in current captures. Treat as fixed envelope/flag content unless future replay work proves otherwise.";

BO_ 43 CHASSIS_STATE_CANDIDATE: 17 BMW_I3
 SG_ CHASSIS_STATE_A : 8|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ CHASSIS_STATE_B : 24|16@1+ (1,0) [0|65535] "" BMW_I3
 CM_ SG_ 43 CHASSIS_STATE_A "Experimental secondary dynamic-state frame. It follows longitudinal phase changes across 00000054/55/b3, but is still weaker than 59 and 54 for isolating stock ACC content.";

